1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,300
Legend says two gods
competed for one city.

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:05,975
Athena won it,
with an olive tree.

3
00:00:06,015 --> 00:00:08,935
Around 1900 BC,
people on Crete

4
00:00:08,975 --> 00:00:12,599
build the great
palace of Knossos.

5
00:00:12,639 --> 00:00:16,059
In 508 BC, Athens
tries something new:

6
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:18,712
democracy, where
citizens vote.

7
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:23,092
In 438 BC, the Parthenon
is dedicated to Athena,

8
00:00:23,132 --> 00:00:25,185
high on the Acropolis.

9
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:28,725
In 334 BC, Alexander
the Great sets out,

10
00:00:28,765 --> 00:00:31,501
and conquers all
the way to India.

11
00:00:31,541 --> 00:00:35,946
By 1460, Greece is under
Ottoman rule, for centuries.

12
00:00:35,986 --> 00:00:38,406
In 1830, after a long war,

13
00:00:38,446 --> 00:00:40,602
Greece becomes independent.

14
00:00:40,642 --> 00:00:42,802
In 1896, Athens hosts

15
00:00:42,842 --> 00:00:45,369
the first modern
Olympic Games.

16
00:00:45,409 --> 00:00:48,009
Today, about 10 million
people call Greece home,

17
00:00:48,049 --> 00:00:50,806
between the mountains
and the sea.

18
00:00:50,846 --> 00:00:54,630
Would you have voted in
ancient Athens? Tell us below.

